{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1176732-some-deathlord-ideas-for-storytellers","id":1176732,"title":"Some Deathlord Ideas for Storytellers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-17T02:58:58-08:00","id":1176732,"title":"Some Deathlord Ideas for Storytellers","content":"Been thinking about death a bit lately... IN EXALTED! DEATH IN EXALTED (figured a need to clarify there!) and did some research. That led me to think of some ideas for Deathlords based on a lack of one in the following locations (the other directions have at least one Deathlord influencing the area in some way).<br /> Put simply there is NO Deathlord in:<ul><li>In Creation's South - specifically the Southern Corners (East and West). Life doesn't flourish as much down here, due to the harsh climate, but death is certainly present!<ul><li>The South <b><i>Underworld</i></b> IS inhabited by the <b>First and Forsaken Lion</b>, and <b>Princess Magnificent</b> - but in positions of exile; unable to easily enter Creation).</li> </ul></li> <li>On the Blessed Isle; understandably due to their high Dragon Blood Population. However, an arrogant Deathlord could chose this as a perfect hiding spot to manipulate elements from behind the scenes; maybe even stiring and encouraging the infighting of the Noble Houses?</li> <li>In Yu-Shan; which is even LESS likely than a Deathlord on the Blessed Isle. Yet again, if one could hide here, they could have a means to manipulate the Loom of Fate, or even work their way through the Celestial Bureaucracy and (in the worst case scenario) win the Games of Divinity for dire consequences!!</li> <li>In Malfeas; which is further unlikely as there is little influence here for one to affect Creation. Its more likely they would exist in Underworld Banishment (like the <b>First and Forsaken Lion</b>, and <b>Princess Magnificent</b>), but maybe there is a plot to turn a Yozi into a new Neverborn - maybe its a loophole in the prison; Yozi's stay, but Neverborn must leave?</li> <li>\u200bIn Autochron; which is divide from creation. Autochron himself is verging on becoming a Neverborn due to his failings, which could result in a Deathlord appearing FROM him. Maybe the hidden 4 are not present, but rather have been &quot;Deathlords Prophesied to Appear?&quot;</li> </ul><br /> Also another thought - while the Liminal Exalted are the result of failed attempts on one of the laws of Magic (the dead do not live again), they are Terrestrial Exalted. As the Abyssals are the result of Corrupted Solar Essences, could a Liminal-Equivilent be made by attempting to create &quot;Death-Blooded Exalted?&quot; - not Ghost-Blooded, but dark Dragon-Blood Equivilents?<br /> <br /> Maybe the &quot;Dark Mother/ Maiden&quot; that the Liminals link themselves to is a Deathlord? Maybe a subtle design created by Princess Magnificent that would go unnoticed by the Neverborn as an escape plan?<br /> <br /> I even had a nice pun for a corrupted &quot;Jade&quot; equivilent - &quot;Deadwood&quot;. Grows in the Underworld, solid like iron-bark or red-wood, made stronger through arificing (maybe lackered with the Essence/ Ecto-plasam of Ghosts?)<br /> <br /> Food for thought anyway....<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T03:43:08-08:00","id":1176738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1176732-some-deathlord-ideas-for-storytellers#post1176732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]In Yu-Shan; which is even LESS likely than a Deathlord on the Blessed Isle. Yet again, if one could hide here, they could have a means to manipulate the Loom of Fate, or even work their way through the Celestial Bureaucracy and (in the worst case scenario) win the Games of Divinity for dire consequences!![*]In Malfeas; which is further unlikely as there is little influence here for one to affect Creation. Its more likely they would exist in Underworld Banishment (like the <b>First and Forsaken Lion</b>, and <b>Princess Magnificent</b>), but maybe there is a plot to turn a Yozi into a new Neverborn - maybe its a loophole in the prison; Yozi's stay, but Neverborn must leave?[*]\u200bIn Autochron; which is divide from creation. Autochron himself is verging on becoming a Neverborn due to his failings, which could result in a Deathlord appearing FROM him. Maybe the hidden 4 are not present, but rather have been &quot;Deathlords Prophesied to Appear?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Deathlords are ghosts, I think they would have a hard time getting into both Yu-Shan and Malfeas. Braving other realms is what they ally with Abyssals for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1176732-some-deathlord-ideas-for-storytellers#post1176732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also another thought - while the Liminal Exalted are the result of failed attempts on one of the laws of Magic (the dead do not live again), they are Terrestrial Exalted. As the Abyssals are the result of Corrupted Solar Essences, could a Liminal-Equivilent be made by attempting to create &quot;Death-Blooded Exalted?&quot; - not Ghost-Blooded, but dark Dragon-Blood Equivilents?<br /> <br /> Maybe the &quot;Dark Mother/ Maiden&quot; that the Liminals link themselves to is a Deathlord? Maybe a subtle design created by Princess Magnificent that would go unnoticed by the Neverborn as an escape plan?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see Liminals as &quot;Dead Exalted.&quot; They are more &quot;<i>Life</i> Exalted.&quot; The Liminals come to be when life is given to where there is death. I fancy the idea of a Dark Mother - Gaia connection more than a Dark Mother - Deathlord connection. The Liminals are basically the opposite of what the Neverborn are striving to create (or unmake).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1176732-some-deathlord-ideas-for-storytellers#post1176732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I even had a nice pun for a corrupted &quot;Jade&quot; equivilent - &quot;Deadwood&quot;. Grows in the Underworld, solid like iron-bark or red-wood, made stronger through arificing (maybe lackered with the Essence/ Ecto-plasam of Ghosts?)</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Dragon-Blooded of different colors mentioned in 2E (The Black Treatise), associated with the five Underworld elements (Ash = Air, Blood = Water, Bone = Wood, Pyre Flame = Fire, Void = Earth). I had some old 2E homebrew for them but don't think it's still around. I may incorporate them into my necromancy homebrew after the DB book hits. If I recall correctly, I think it's mentioned somewhere that there may be Underworld jade too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T03:47:42-08:00","id":1176740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1176732-some-deathlord-ideas-for-storytellers?p=1176738#post1176738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Deathlords are ghosts, I think they would have a hard time getting into both Yu-Shan and Malfeas. Braving other realms is what they ally with Abyssals for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see that being ghosts makes it harder. In 2nd ed, there were a bunch of ghosts in Malfeas (mostly Yozi cultists). Being in Yu-Shan is a lot more problematic, but not specifically because they're ghosts (though perhaps because they're Creatures of Darkness).<br /> <br /> <br /> Of the two, one being in Malfeas seems much more plausible than one being in Yu-Shan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T04:32:23-08:00","id":1176745,"title":"","content":"I agree with you both. And the idea behind it isn't &quot;is it east&quot; but rather... what could happen if they did?<br /> <br /> Its kinda like the Solars. The Impossible and Unlikely are made into reality. And while Deathlords aren't Solars, the entire world is about creating &quot;what if&quot; scenarios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T10:19:13-08:00","id":1176798,"title":"","content":"I think you are trying to bring 2nd Edition Deathlord lore into 3e where it doesn't need to be, nor is desirable. The idea of all the Deathlords having malign interests in Creation isn't really a good one. It leads to the existential doom syndrome that plagued 2e writing, where all of Creation needs to unite to defeat a million threats to the entire world.<br /> <br /> \u200b3e has even unshackled itself from the idea that the Deathlords are Usurpation-killed Solars hopped up on dead Yozi souls. Now, the Deathlords can just be incredibly powerful and ancient ghosts of any stripe, some with absolutely no desire to invade Creation in any way and which are perfectly happy to play out their melodramas and intrigues in Underworld kingdoms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T11:16:33-08:00","id":1176806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1176732-some-deathlord-ideas-for-storytellers?p=1176798#post1176798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are trying to bring 2nd Edition Deathlord lore into 3e where it doesn't need to be, nor is desirable. The idea of all the Deathlords having malign interests in Creation isn't really a good one. It leads to the existential doom syndrome that plagued 2e writing, where all of Creation needs to unite to defeat a million threats to the entire world.<br /> <br /> \u200b3e has even unshackled itself from the idea that the Deathlords are Usurpation-killed Solars hopped up on dead Yozi souls. Now, the Deathlords can just be incredibly powerful and ancient ghosts of any stripe, some with absolutely no desire to invade Creation in any way and which are perfectly happy to play out their melodramas and intrigues in Underworld kingdoms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oooh. If thats true, i like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Where is this written?<br /> <br /> I know a few Exalted ideas are being thrown out the window (the &quot;ONE TRUTH&quot; of the scarlet Empresse' disappearance for one), though I didn't find MANY of the Deathlords to be immanent Threats... the Silver Prince being the only one that seemed on the verge of something big.<br /> <br /> Besides these ideas don't touch on the Lore but rather general location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T11:23:50-08:00","id":1176807,"title":"","content":"In general I agree with the OP's point that Deathlords and their servants should be things encounterable in the world, and the lack of one with interests in the South does feel like a real lack (especially now that the Southeast is a real place). However, I agree strongly with Kyeudo that they shouldn't all be obviously evil/have necessarily malign interests. 1e Silver Prince, for example, makes a good example of a creepy-but-not-Skeletor dude who makes the area around him more interesting and is an entity with whom player characters can have a variety of interactions: he's got a set of goals that don't necessarily support or contradict PC goals, and therefore might be someone they work for, against, or alongside (or all three at different times!).<br /> <br /> Also this is tangential but I love Eye and Seven Despairs and his utter dedication to being completely ineffectual at anything that isn't &quot;furthering his personal angst.&quot; He's grandly petty, if that makes any sense, in the best tradition of gothic melodrama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T11:37:25-08:00","id":1176808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1176732-some-deathlord-ideas-for-storytellers?p=1176798#post1176798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are trying to bring 2nd Edition Deathlord lore into 3e where it doesn't need to be, nor is desirable. The idea of all the Deathlords having malign interests in Creation isn't really a good one. It leads to the existential doom syndrome that plagued 2e writing, where all of Creation needs to unite to defeat a million threats to the entire world.<br /> <br /> \u200b3e has even unshackled itself from the idea that the Deathlords are Usurpation-killed Solars hopped up on dead Yozi souls. Now, the Deathlords can just be incredibly powerful and ancient ghosts of any stripe, some with absolutely no desire to invade Creation in any way and which are perfectly happy to play out their melodramas and intrigues in Underworld kingdoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the devs have confirmed the Deathlords, or at least the greatest of the Deathlords that the Abyssal Charmset echoes, are still the bitter ghosts of Usurpation slain Solars. But the whole \u201chave a helatonchire shoved in them\u201d thing is indeed supposed to be gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T12:20:58-08:00","id":1176815,"title":"","content":"One thing I like about the Deathlords (and many others things put out by Onyxpath/white wolf) is the fact that we have a lot of examples of them and how they differ from one another and how they are alike. Since we have those examples but there are several Deathlords left completely unexplained leaving us with plenty of creative potential. For example one of my players is a reincarnation of Brigid/Salanin. He is a sorcerer of course and has a lot of talent for it but has strong negative opinions against Necromancy. That led me to create a custom Deathlord who goes by the title of The Black Crone who was the previous incarnation of that exaltation. I've used them now as an antagonist once and their powerful connection to magic wielding powerful sorcery and necromancy casually has managed to tempt one of the other players to bargains and seeding the fun risk of serious party conflict in the future. I look forward to seeing the fallout of the Zenith dumping that potion into the well of a southern city. It should be beautifully dramatic. My point is a lot of the areas are left &quot;untouched&quot; by Deathlords so that the ST can make the decision to use whatever antagonists they desire, and the undefined Deathlords are rich for creative opportunities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T20:10:44-08:00","id":1176882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1176732-some-deathlord-ideas-for-storytellers?p=1176808#post1176808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the devs have confirmed the Deathlords, or at least the greatest of the Deathlords that the Abyssal Charmset echoes, are still the bitter ghosts of Usurpation slain Solars. But the whole \u201chave a helatonchire shoved in them\u201d thing is indeed supposed to be gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not surprised that the ones most obsessed with Creation are jilted Solars. I just like the extra room to have the Dual Monarchs as Deathlords and completely uninterested in destroying anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1176732-some-deathlord-ideas-for-storytellers?p=1176806#post1176806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooh. If thats true, i like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Where is this written?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more about what is not written. Go reread 3e's section on the Deathlords. Look for what isn't said. Contrast it to the 2e core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know a few Exalted ideas are being thrown out the window (the &quot;ONE TRUTH&quot; of the scarlet Empresse' disappearance for one), though I didn't find MANY of the Deathlords to be immanent Threats... the Silver Prince being the only one that seemed on the verge of something big. </div> </div> </div>Let's see what 2e had as doomsday plans:<br /> <br /> The First and Forsaken Lion has an army so large that it can readily conquer the whole of the South but the Lion can't find a shadowland big enough to use as a beachhead. He's got a soulsteel version of those First Age Independence Day doom beams under construction. He'll probably slaughter Gem to create that beachhead.<br /> <br /> The Dowager is looking into the Well of Udr and will eventually roll around to something as devastating as the Great Contagion again. Could be tomorrow, could be next century.<br /> <br /> Bodhisattva Anointed By Dark Water is building the fleet of doom on Isle 4 and will use it to conquer the oceans.<br /> <br /> The Bishop of the Chalcedony Thurible is distilling a nihilistic doctrine that will cause anyone who hears it to commit suicide and plunge their ghost into Oblivion.<br /> <br /> The Lover Clad In the Raiment of Tears is about to destroy Lookshy using a doomsday device built into a soulsteel warstrider, destabilizing the power balance of the Eastern Threshold.<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters has the single largest army in the Scavenger Lands, kept from moving on any of its neighbors by the military might of Lookshy.<br /> <br /> The Eye and Seven Despairs has already created a doomsday plague that will basically unleash a zombie apocalypse across Creation, but lost track of it because he's engaged in sadistic games with his deathknights. If he ever pulled his head out of his personal vendetta, he might notice that it's been stolen or he might decide that he doesn't care because the container will eventually leak (as it is doing currently)<br /> <br /> The Walker In Darkness and the Princess Magnificent are the only two Deathlords who don't have a doomsday plan about to go off and conquer at least a whole direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T02:11:26-08:00","id":1176911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1176732-some-deathlord-ideas-for-storytellers?p=1176882#post1176882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more about what is not written. Go reread 3e's section on the Deathlords. Look for what isn't said. Contrast it to the 2e core.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also a few comments in passing in the Ask the Dev thread as to how the Deathlords are being revised so they can <i>function</i> as mentors to PCs, so that there will be interest in playing loyalist abyssals.<br /> <br /> Eye and Seven Despairs is being revised as a proper gothic mad scientist, and Princess Magnificent with Lips of Coral and Robes of Black Feathers is having hear built as an elegant yet savage assassin.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]